SetReplicasTempMapRange	inadmissible	appends to or inserts into m[k], not a field path of a pointer parameter the body never reassigns or takes the address of; class a is F = append(F, v) or F[k] = v on such a path (purity §4)
SetReplicasTempSliceExpanded	inadmissible	xs := []string{…} is not v, err := json.Marshal(P) with two new names and P a parameter other than the object (grammar S3, purity §4)
SetReplicasThenReturn	inadmissible	returns early instead of writing; a nil receiver panics and sugar has no conditional no-op (purity §4)
SetReplicasThroughStar	pointer	pointer-typed field assignment (class b)
SetReplicasTupleReroot	inadmissible	p, p.Spec.Replicas = o, &n is not one target assigned one value with = (grammar S7, purity §4)
SetReplicasTwoObjects	inadmissible	b.Spec.Name is spelled from b, not from a, the object of the first write (grammar P1, purity §4)
SetReplicasUnusedInit	inadmissible	the nil-init of o.Labels is not written through (grammar P6, purity §4)
SetReplicasValidated	inadmissible	if n < 0 is not a nil guard that panics, the guard on the error of a local, or a nil-init guard (grammar S8, purity §4)
SetReplicasViaAddr	inadmissible	pp := &o is not v, err := json.Marshal(P) with two new names and P a parameter other than the object (grammar S3, purity §4)
SetReplicasViaAlias	inadmissible	a declaration is neither an if nor an assignment (grammar S1, purity §4)
SetReplicasViaClosure	inadmissible	contains a function literal; its body is not checked, so sugar has none
SetReplicasZero	inadmissible	writes a value the caller did not supply to o.Spec.Replicas (purity §4)
SetSpecNestedNil	inadmissible	assigns nil to o.Spec.Ref, a field the caller did not name (purity §4)
SetSpecWithNilRef	inadmissible	assigns nil to o.Spec.Ref, a field the caller did not name (purity §4)
SetViaDelegate	inadmissible	no field write (delegation or no-op)
